From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: give the first scan the full completion budget

Background scanning may alternate short channel visits with home-channel
service. A short initial watchdog can abort every valid long scan before a
successful completion grants the longer timeout. Use the existing bounded
30-second completion budget from the first accepted request. Completion and
abort events still cancel it immediately; no-event fallback stays finite.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
---

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_scan.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_scan.c
@@ -455,19 +455,12 @@
 	}
 
 	drv->scan_state = SCAN_REQUESTED;
-	/* Not all drivers generate "scan completed" wireless event, so try to
-	 * read results after a timeout. */
-	timeout = drv->uses_6ghz ? 20 : 10;
-	if (drv->uses_s1g)
-		timeout += 5;
-	if (drv->scan_complete_events) {
-		/*
-		 * The driver seems to deliver events to notify when scan is
-		 * complete, so use longer timeout to avoid race conditions
-		 * with scanning and following association request.
-		 */
-		timeout = 30;
-	}
+	/* Background scans can spend most of their time servicing the home
+	 * channel. Give the first scan the same bounded completion budget as
+	 * later event-completed scans; a short initial watchdog can abort every
+	 * valid long scan before the driver ever reports its first completion.
+	 * Drivers without completion events still have a finite fallback. */
+	timeout = 30;
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "Scan requested (ret=%d) - scan timeout %d "
 		   "seconds", ret, timeout);
 	eloop_cancel_timeout(wpa_driver_nl80211_scan_timeout, drv, bss->ctx);
